==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|perturben|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|fro}} {{term|perturber|lang=fro}}, from {{etyl|la}} {{term|perturbare||throw into confusion, confuse, disorder, disturb|lang=la}}, from {{term|per||through}} + {{term|lang=la|turbare||to confuse, disturb}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-perturb.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|ɜː(r)b}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To [[disturb]]; to bother or unsettle.
# {{physics}} To slightly modify the motion of an object.
# {{astronomy}} To modify the motion of a body by exerting a gravitational force.
# {{mathematics}} To modify slightly, such as an equation or value.

====Derived terms====
* [[perturbation]]
* [[perturbative]]

